https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120424#issuecomment-4756987934","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120424","id":4756987934,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG4ngHg","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-20T08:20:25Z","updated_at":"2026-06-20T08:20:25Z","body":"Unless I am missing something, we don't need to add extra properties to lock the PinJoint2D.\r\n\r\nJust set both limits to the same number (0.0) and it should lock. This is how the 6DOF joint currently works (and will likely work in future: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14845)\r\n\r\nOf course limits are not working, nor is the motor, but I have a full PinJoint2D fix locally which works as I described.\r\n\r\nSo I would request that you don't merge this, and rather wait a few days or weeks for a holistic fix which doesn't add properties.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4756987934/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4767012428","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120424#issuecomment-4767012428","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120424","id":4767012428,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHCLWTA","user":{"login":"Marenz","id":424752,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNDc1Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/424752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz","html_url":"https://github.com/Marenz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marenz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-22T09:50:14Z","updated_at":"2026-06-22T09:51:19Z","body":"> but I have a full PinJoint2D fix locally which works as I described.\r\n\r\nI have tried a lot of things and in regards to the `PinJoint2D`, nothing worked reliably for me. Certainly not setting the limits accordingly. I'd be happy & curious to see your implementation, maybe I can break it and we can make it stable. Or maybe its all I need, but then the discussion on https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/86 seems to be out-to-date in terms of what works or not. (Edit: Misread, you said its not working currently but you have a fix)\r\n\r\nI did however use the same techniques regarding solving that are used in the 3D variant. They seemed to be the least-disruptive variant to implement it. \r\n\r\n> Please describe what parts of the code was not authored by you as per the guidelines\r\n\r\nIt was developed in an interactive session with prompts, reviews and tests to shape the code and commits. I didn't manually write code for this (I generally don't do that anymore).","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4767012428/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4794875893","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120424#issuecomment-4794875893","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120424","id":4794875893,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHcv_9Q","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-25T00:52:08Z","updated_at":"2026-06-25T00:52:08Z","body":"> I'd be happy & curious to see your implementation, maybe I can break it and we can make it stable. Or maybe its all I need, but then the discussion on [godotengine/godot-proposals#86](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/86) seems to be out-to-date in terms of what works or not. (Edit: Misread, you said its not working currently but you have a fix)\r\n\r\nThanks, it's finally done:\r\n[Fix PinJoint2D limits and motor #120623](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120623)\r\n\r\nAny testing you could do would be fantastic! \r\n\r\nTo turn the PinJoint2D into a weld/fixed joint:\r\n- Turn on limits\r\n- Set both limits to 0\r\n- Set softness to 0.0 (unless you want more give)\r\n\r\nThese settings should reduce the code down to a Fixed/Weld joint. Further user settings required to optimise the lock as below:\r\n* Try setting a higher bias on the locking joint (can get jittery if too high)\r\n* Drop your default contact bias in settings down to 0.1-0.3 (not 0.8)\r\n* Match masses and mass distributions between the locked bodies.\r\n* Higher masses on the locked bodies so they don't get pushed around easily\r\n\r\n## Future considerations\r\nJoint based locking could be perfected by making that joint the last constraint in the solver list. The last row in the solver has no other constraints running after it (which could otherwise force new errors on the joint). There is minimal cost to this little trick, compared to creating compound bodies like I hear Roblox does, but it is an engine specific trick, and needs to expose settings somehow. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4794875893/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4860000305","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120424#issuecomment-4860000305","issue_url":"https: